# Governs what `gcloud builds submit` uploads as build context — separate
# from .dockerignore (which only governs what the Dockerfile's `docker
# build` step sees once the source has already landed on Cloud Build).
# Without this file, gcloud does NOT reliably auto-derive from .gitignore,
# and ends up uploading things like .venv/ (~1GB, tens of thousands of
# files) on every single build submission — this was silently ballooning
# each build's upload step even though the Dockerfile never touches .venv/.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
outputs/
.venv/
venv/
.chroma/
.voice_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
tests/
finetune/
apps/
examples/
docs/
scratch_check/
*.ipynb
*.zip
.mcp.json
# *.png excludes stray screenshots at repo root, but the Dockerfile now
# COPYs assets/ (for the PWA favicon, see Section 11.7) — un-exclude it so
# `gcloud builds submit` actually uploads that file to Cloud Build.
*.png
!assets/*.png
